WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.200
Less than three years ago, I was using a camera for the first time.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.200
Now I've filmed John Mayer, Billie Joe Armstrong,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.960
Robbie Krieger from The Doors,

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.200
and worked with all kinds of different brands.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.100
I spent so many hours watching YouTube videos and chasing rabbits down holes,

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.430
but what really helped me learn was learning from real people,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.570
mentors who could watch what I was doing and guide me in the right directions.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.210
There were so many moments where I learned a seemingly small concept,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.120
and it made a massive difference in the results I was seeing.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.640
So I built Velo with the help of my team of talented humans,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.160
by the way, not AI,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.200
to pack all those most important concepts into a short, guided, interactive course.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.050
Whether you're a complete beginner who's touching a camera for the

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.060
first time, or maybe you've been at it for a year or so and are just

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.840
feeling like you're still missing out on some of your best results,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.560
these interactive lessons will help you become a better photographer or videographer.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.160
This is not a video course.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.510
We've actually designed and built a custom software that will teach

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.440
you through interactive lessons.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.490
You can click through camera settings or effects and see what's

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:05.920
changing in real time.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.440
You can compare a photo with or without an effect that you're learning about.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.640
You can also learn your camera's manual mode settings super quickly

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.770
with our camera simulator exercises,

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:18.480
so you'll know exactly how to get what's in your head out of it and

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.600
into the camera.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.410
And yes, there are short videos for each chapter if you learn better

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.570
that way, but each one will include different example materials and

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.280
wording from the interactive reading lessons to make sure you're

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.520
really understanding the materials.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.800
Click the link below to learn more.
